      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b64131d7f033f28768aaa73|full_name}: Writing GiB doesn't confuse anyone, because it only means one thing. Writing GB is confusing because it means two different things and you have to guess which one the author might have meant.\n\nMy default assumption is that it means 1000, and just because Windows is written by people who are incapable of following the international standard, in a country filled with people incapable of following international standards, doesn't mean that it's correct for everyone else to follow their lead.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
